import MaxCaterpillar.SmallN.Max4Test
import MaxCaterpillar.SmallN.Max5General4
import MaxCaterpillar.SmallN.Max5Lns27

/-! # Exact small-arity expansions of the maximum (generated certificates)

Each instance `MaxCaterpillar.SmallN.<Name>` proves `max_identity` (an explicit
identity for `Maximum N` on all of `ℝ^N`) and `max_network` (a two-hidden-layer
network with the paper's first hidden layer, rational weights, zero biases).
The sources are generated by `scripts/smalln/gen_lean.py`; see
`scripts/smalln/README.md`.

* `Max4Test`: `SmallArity.max_four_identity` regenerated through the pipeline,
  widths `(firstWidth 4, 5)`.
* `Max5General4`: four general second-layer neurons, widths `(firstWidth 5, 6)`.
* `Max5Lns27`: 27 caterpillar functions, widths `(firstWidth 5, 29)`.
-/
